contentText:
One thing about Jim Jones ? He&#8217;s good for a quote.

The Harlem rapper popped by the No Funny Sh&#8211; podcast recently and was asked about the Verzuz challenge he made toward his fellow Diplomat Cam&#8217;ron back in May. And while he acknowledged that the challenge was just him trolling a little bit, Jimmy also said that he feels like he has one of the better discographies in New York rap history.

“I got a better catalog than over 90 percent of the rappers out of New York City in history,&#8221; he said confidently. &#8220;Not to be like&#8230;there&#8217;s been a lot of rappers in New York, but I got real gold records, more than one of them, like albums and sh&#8211; like that. You dig? I got real platinum singles and sh&#8211; like that.&#8221;

He added: &#8220;Some of your favorite rappers don&#8217;t have nothing platinum. That doesn&#8217;t make me better than anybody and sh&#8211; like that, but statistically I got a hell of a catalog. I mean, from every album that I put out, I got a dope a&#8211; single, especially in New York. In New York, hands down, I know I got 20 records.&#8221;

Jim made headlines this time last year when he defended himself after a podcast clip of a college student saying the Dipset member was more relevant than Nas went viral. However, during an interview with the legendary Angie Martinez , Jones admitted that he didn&#8217;t realize how many fans the Queens rapper still has after his comments received massive pushback from the hip-hop community.

